(GLOBAL MASTER SERVICES AGREEMENT) '
() '
(This Master Services Agreement \("Agreement"\) is dated as of October 1, 2026 \("Effective Date"\), by and between:) '
() '
(Party A: Apex Infrastructure Global Corp., a Delaware corporation with offices at 100 Enterprise Way, Suite 400, New York, NY \("Service Provider"\), and) '
(Party B: Meridian Enterprise Technologies, LLC, a California limited liability company with offices at 500 Market Street, San Francisco, CA \("Customer"\).) '
() '
(RECITALS) '
(WHEREAS, Customer desires to retain Service Provider to perform enterprise software implementation, infrastructure analysis, and continuous monitoring services; and) '
(WHEREAS, Service Provider possesses specialized technical expertise and agrees to provide such services under the terms and conditions set forth herein.) '
() '
(NOW, THEREFORE, in consideration of the mutual covenants and conditions contained herein, the parties agree as follows:) '
() '
(1. DEFINITIONS AND INTERPRETATION) '
() '
(1.1 "Affiliate" means any entity that directly or indirectly controls, is controlled by, or is under common control with a party.) '
() '
(1.2 "Applicable Law" means all international, federal, state, and local statutes, ordinances, regulations, and judicial orders.) '
() '
(1.3 "Authorized User" means an individual employee, agent, or independent contractor authorized by Customer to access the Platform.) '
() '
(1.4 "Claim" means any third-party civil, criminal, administrative, or investigative demand, lawsuit, arbitration, or proceeding.) '
() '
(1.5 "Confidential Information" means all non-public information disclosed by either party, whether in tangible, electronic, or oral form.) '
() '
(1.6 "Customer Data" means all electronic data, documents, files, and records submitted, uploaded, or transmitted by Customer.) '
() '
() '
ET
endstream
endobj
